    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#finland">Finland</a> declared independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#russia">Russia</a> on 6 December 1917 and became a republic with the constitution of 1919.</li><li>It fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in the Winter War and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#continuation-war">Continuation War</a>, losing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#karelia">Karelia</a> but keeping its independence.</li><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#cold-war">Cold War</a> neutral, it joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#european-union">European Union</a> in 1995, adopted the euro in 1999 and joined NATO in 2023.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The parliamentary reform of 1906 made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#finland">Finland</a> the first country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a> where women could both vote and stand for parliament; nineteen women were elected in 1907.</p></aside>
    </section>

